<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">CONTROLLED EXPERIMENT · SPA ACCESSIBILITY</div><h1>Conformance Testing<br><span>Laboratory</span></h1><p>Compare authored DOM evidence with the browser-computed Accessibility Tree across repeatable single-page application scenarios.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#register">Explore test cases</a><a class="button secondary" href="/api/cases">View case register ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="run-console" aria-labelledby="run-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">EXPERIMENT CONTROL</div><h2 id="run-heading">Run the paired experiment</h2><p>Execute both engines across the 24 interim variants for five repetitions, plus separate axe-core reference scans. The runner saves raw JSON/CSV, dynamic-scenario evidence, and automatic keyboard/focus-order checks for TC08 and TC15.</p></div><div class="run-actions"><button class="button primary" id="run-experiment" type="button">Run five-repeat experiment</button><button class="button secondary" id="refresh-runs" type="button">Refresh history</button></div><p id="run-status" class="run-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready. Expected labels remain provisional until independently reviewed.</p><div id="run-history" class="run-history" aria-label="Previous experiment runs"></div></section>
<section class="notice" role="note"><strong>Research integrity notice</strong><p>All expected labels are provisional fixture intentions. They are not validated ground truth and must not be used to claim accuracy until each case has been independently reviewed and documented.</p></section>
<section class="stats" aria-label="Experiment overview"><article><span class="stat-number">{{families.length}}</span><span>Test families</span></article><article><span class="stat-number">{{totalCases}}</span><span>Variants</span></article><article><span class="stat-number">2</span><span>Independent engines</span></article><article><span class="stat-number">240</span><span>Paired engine evaluations</span></article></section>
<section class="section-head" id="register"><div><div class="eyebrow">TEST REGISTER</div><h2>Scenario catalogue</h2><p>Each family includes two seeded defective variants and one intended compliant control.</p></div><input id="case-search" type="search" placeholder="Search test families…" aria-label="Search test families"></section>
<div class="family-grid" id="family-grid">{{#each families}}<article class="family-card" data-search="{{id}} {{name}} {{wcag}}"><div class="card-top"><span class="case-id">{{id}}</span><span class="wcag">WCAG {{wcag}}</span></div><h3>{{name}}</h3><p>{{description}}</p><div class="variants"><a class="variant-link defect" href="/test/{{id}}-D1" aria-label="Open {{id}} defective variant one">D1</a><a class="variant-link defect" href="/test/{{id}}-D2" aria-label="Open {{id}} defective variant two">D2</a><a class="variant-link control" href="/test/{{id}}-C" aria-label="Open {{id}} compliant control">C</a></div><div class="card-foot"><span>3 variants · 2 engines</span><span>Open a variant ↑</span></div></article>{{/each}}</div>
<section class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">EXPERIMENT PIPELINE</div><h2>How the comparison works</h2></div></section>
<div class="pipeline"><div><b>01</b><strong>Reset scenario</strong><span>Same route, browser and interaction state</span></div><div><b>02</b><strong>DOM engine</strong><span>DOM checks plus real Playwright Tab/Enter/Space and focus-order interactions</span></div><div><b>03</b><strong>Tree engine</strong><span>Chromium CDP full AX tree evidence</span></div><div><b>04</b><strong>Record & analyse</strong><span>JSON, CSV, coverage and metrics</span></div></div>
